# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
# Mustfile — Enaction Engine hard invariants

@abstract:
Release-blocking invariants for the implemented deterministic substrate,
canonical identity, licence posture, and honest architecture claims.
@end

## Deterministic substrate

### whole-steps-only
- description: Simulation support exposes whole equal steps; alpha is presentation-only
- run: cargo test --workspace
- severity: critical

### interpolation-render-only
- description: Documentation and host examples prohibit sampled values from re-entering simulation
- run: grep -q 'render-only' README.adoc && grep -q 'render interpolation never feeds simulation state' ARCHITECTURE.md
- severity: critical

### discontinuity-commit-then-snap
- description: Tests pin commit followed by snap for discontinuities
- run: cargo test --workspace commit_then_snap
- severity: critical

## Project identity

### workspace-loads
- description: The workspace manifest is valid and every member resolves
- run: cargo metadata --format-version 1 --no-deps >/dev/null
- severity: critical
- notes: |
  This is the check that was missing. The previous invariant grepped for one
  exact members line, which said nothing about whether the members existed.
  A merge landed a members entry pointing at a directory with no Cargo.toml,
  and `cargo metadata` failed for a day while the grep-based checks reported
  only that the string had changed.

  Assert the property, not the spelling.

### canonical-repository
- description: Cargo repository metadata uses the canonical repository URL
- run: grep -q 'https://github.com/metadatastician/enaction-engine' Cargo.toml
- severity: critical

### crate-admission
- description: Every crates/ subdirectory is a real, named, declared package (ADR-0017)
- run: for d in crates/*/; do n=$(basename "$d"); case "$n" in enaction-*) ;; *) exit 1 ;; esac; test -f "$d/Cargo.toml" && test -d "$d/src" || exit 1; { test -d "$d/tests" || grep -rq '#\[cfg(test)\]' "$d/src"; } || exit 1; grep -q "crates/$n" Cargo.toml || exit 1; done
- severity: critical
- notes: |
  Replaces a crate-count check that asserted exactly one directory under
  crates/. A count is a fake check the moment the number legitimately
  changes, and it had already rotted: it failed because a half-finished
  rename left an empty directory behind, which is not what it was written
  to detect.

  This asserts the rule ADR-0012 actually meant -- no empty facades, no
  namespace reservations, no undeclared members -- and needs no editing when
  a fourth crate legitimately arrives.

  Tests may live in tests/ or inline as #[cfg(test)] in src/. ADR-0012
  requires "tests or another proportionate verification gate", not a
  particular directory layout: enaction-trace tests inline, and an
  earlier draft of this check wrongly failed it for that.

### rust-formatted
- description: The workspace is rustfmt-clean
- run: cargo fmt --all -- --check
- severity: critical
- notes: Unreachable while the workspace manifest was broken, since rustfmt
  could not load it. Drift could have accumulated invisibly.

### accelerator-conformance-digests
- description: Versioned accelerator inputs and expected outputs match their accepted digests
- run: cd conformance/accelerator/v1 && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
- severity: critical

## Verified native interface seam

### idris2-abi-typechecks
- description: Idris2 remains the normative, typechecked ABI source
- run: idris2 --typecheck abi.ipkg
- severity: critical

### idris2-abi-no-unsound-escapes
- description: The accelerator ABI authority contains no Idris2 trust-me escape hatch
- run: test -z "$(grep -En 'believe_me|assert_total|postulate' src/interface/Abi/Accelerator.idr src/interface/Abi/Generate.idr || true)"
- severity: critical

### accelerator-abi-generated-current
- description: C-compatible, Zig and Rust declarations reproduce byte-for-byte from the Idris2 authority
- run: scripts/generate-accelerator-abi.sh --check
- severity: critical

### accelerator-abi-source-digests
- description: Generated ABI provenance names the exact accepted Idris2 sources
- run: sha256sum -c src/interface/generated/abi/SOURCE.sha256
- severity: critical

### zig-ffi-formatted
- description: The Zig FFI implementation and tests remain formatter-clean
- run: zig fmt --check src/interface/ffi/src/main.zig src/interface/ffi/src/accelerator.zig src/interface/ffi/build.zig src/interface/ffi/test/integration_test.zig src/interface/generated/abi/enaction_accelerator.zig
- severity: critical

### zig-ffi-tests
- description: The pure Zig FFI implementation passes its native tests
- run: ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=target/zig-global-cache ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR=target/zig-local-cache zig test src/interface/ffi/src/main.zig
- severity: critical

### zig-accelerator-tests
- description: The Idris2-defined pure-Zig kernels pass exact and planted-failure tests
- run: ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=target/zig-global-cache ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR=target/zig-accelerator-cache zig test --dep abi -Mroot=src/interface/ffi/src/accelerator.zig -Mabi=src/interface/generated/abi/enaction_accelerator.zig
- severity: critical

### zig-ffi-build
- description: The real Zig build graph runs every FFI test and produces a ReleaseSafe library
- run: cd src/interface/ffi && ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=../../../target/zig-global-cache ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR=../../../target/zig-build-cache zig build test && ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=../../../target/zig-global-cache ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR=../../../target/zig-build-cache zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe
- severity: critical

### accelerator-abi-symbols
- description: The ReleaseSafe Zig library exports exactly the Idris2-declared accelerator symbol set
- run: nm -g --defined-only src/interface/ffi/zig-out/lib/libenaction_accelerator.a | awk '$2 == "T" && $3 ~ /^enaction_accel_/ { print $3 }' | sort | diff - src/interface/generated/abi/SYMBOLS
- severity: critical

### no-handwritten-c-ffi
- description: C is an ABI convention and generated declaration format, not an FFI implementation language
- run: test -z "$(find src/interface/ffi -type f \( -name '*.c' -o -name '*.cc' -o -name '*.cpp' \) -print -quit)"
- severity: critical

## Evidence and governance

### principal-documents
- description: README, EXPLAINME, architecture, roadmap, UMS integration, and ADRs exist
- run: test -f README.adoc && test -f EXPLAINME.adoc && test -f ARCHITECTURE.md && test -f docs/status/ROADMAP.adoc && test -f docs/architecture/UMS-INTEGRATION.adoc && test -f docs/decisions/0012-no-speculative-subsystems.adoc
- severity: critical

### licence-content
- description: Root licence remains the full GNU AGPL version 3 text
- run: grep -q 'GNU AFFERO GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE' LICENSE
- severity: critical

### no-untracked-contractiles
- description: Contractile files are tracked before release
- run: test -z "$(git ls-files -o --exclude-standard .machine_readable/contractiles/)"
- severity: critical

### signed-release-commit
- description: A release commit must carry a valid Git signature
- run: git verify-commit HEAD
- severity: critical
